WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.100
<i>...spring, now the flower blooms</i>

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:02.980
Yoshino
 Tournament

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:02.980
Round 2

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.860
<b>Registered Architects 
1st Class License Course 

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:08.750
This year's competition is 
way more heated than usual.

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:11.870
We have all the big names,
but also youngsters on the rise.

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:14.020
High schoolers sure are formidable.

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:15.880
I wonder who's going to win.

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:17.850
The Nagumo Society's gonna go places.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:20.820
Yeah, but the one drawing 
the most attention is...

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:27.900
Inokuma Haruka, grade 6,

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:31.590
the former queen returning from maternity 
leave, who once won four years in a row.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.290
And her eyes are still huge!

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:34.640
Scary huge!

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:41.140
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:42.970
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:47.200
Aki! Jin!

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:48.910
Mommy won!

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:52.250
Verse 3

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:52.250
But from
the crystal
 white
 snow of 
Yoshino

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:51.220
Sorry I had a little trouble.

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:53.330
Mama! Mama!

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:53.330
Hungry, Jin?

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:55.150
Just a second...

00:01:56.080 --> 00:02:00.340
It's impressive that you can play 
karuta with a baby still nursing.

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:01.860
Sakurazawa-san!

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:03.580
You stopped wearing contacts?

00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:07.310
I wasn't taking good care of them, 
so the doctor said to stop.

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:09.510
You're breastfeeding now? Right here?

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:11.610
I manage surprisingly well with the kid.

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:15.690
I even feed him during my fifteen-minute 
memorization time at practice.

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:18.220
Come on, Jin! Eat fast!

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:19.670
Guzzle it down!

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:25.900
It really takes passion 
to come back to the game.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:32.080
<i>The fall wind parts the wispy clouds</i>

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:30.710
Thank you very much.

00:02:38.150 --> 00:02:39.870
Chihaya-chan, you won!

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:40.740
It's lunchtime.

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:41.980
We've got chocolate.

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:42.920
Thanks!

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:46.190
How'd the second round go?

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:49.010
Well, he touched "While the" 
when it was "While I"

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:51.950
and didn't attack on "Would this,"
so it felt like I slid into the win.

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:53.260
Slid into it?

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:54.820
How's your right hand?

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:57.380
My right hand...

00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:00.170
She fell asleep!

00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:02.530
Chihaya-chan, you're going to fall!

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:03.900
She always does this.

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:05.170
Just let her sleep.

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:09.280
<i>Ayase's right hand isn't 
back to full strength yet.</i>

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:12.310
<i>Her swings didn't have their 
usual force and strength.</i>

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:15.800
<i>I guess that's to be expected 
so soon after surgery.</i>

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:19.280
Where's President Mashima, anyway?

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:34.640
What song is that?

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:37.050
A-Arata!

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:40.410
Sorry to interrupt your break. 
I heard you humming.

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:42.330
I-It's...

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:45.910
<b>Mizusawa High 
School Song
Lyrics: Karuta Inochi</b>

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:45.910
1. 
The bells ring in the streets of Mizuha 
For this brilliant house of learning 
Hope is far in the distance 
We hold the will to win in our hearts 
As Mizusawa High walks forth 

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:44.590
It's just our school song.

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:46.760
I get it.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:47.960
You do?!

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:50.000
When you're playing multiple matches,

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:53.230
you have to get creative
 to reset your memory.

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:55.920
I always do math exercises.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:57.950
Y-Yeah?

00:03:57.950 --> 00:04:00.750
What about memorization 
during matches, then?

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:01.550
Huh?

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:03.260
How do you do it?

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:05.180
Well...

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:09.680
Starting with the one-syllable cards,
I look over all 50 three or four times.

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:12.210
The rest is predicting strategies—

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:15.810
how the hands will move
and how the layout could change.

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:19.160
Exactly! The cards are in different 
places by the end, right?

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:20.150
Yep.

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:21.620
So when they move,

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:24.650
I forget the initial layout 
and memorize the current one.

00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:25.450
Huh?!

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:27.880
Y-You can actually do that?

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:31.830
Yeah. When I try to update 
what I've already memorized,

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:33.030
I just get lost.

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:34.690
<i>Huh...</i>

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:38.300
<i>Oh, this feels weird...</i>

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:42.590
<i>There's so much I want 
to talk to Arata about.</i>

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:46.100
<i>So many things... through karuta.</i>

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:48.270
Taichi.

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:53.090
You know, um... I mean...

00:04:53.550 --> 00:04:55.780
Was it hard to start a karuta club?

00:04:57.250 --> 00:04:58.190
Huh?

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:03.280
I talked to some people, and the Nagumo 
Society gained some new members,

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:05.570
but no one wants to play at school.

00:05:06.190 --> 00:05:09.470
I'd like to get at least five 
members, like Mizusawa.

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:14.590
If I could get four, or even just three, 
we could play in team matches...

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:16.880
<i>Team matches?</i>

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:21.700
<i>He wants to play team matches, too?</i>

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:28.650
It was mostly Chihaya being so pushy 
that brought our club together.

00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:30.060
There was no trick to it.

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:33.480
So it was Chihaya... Makes sense.

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:35.840
Chihaya's pretty amazing.

00:05:37.610 --> 00:05:40.470
I thought you were focusing
solely on a Master match.

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:44.490
Guess you're feeling confident.

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:51.090
<i>What's my problem?</i>

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:53.860
<i>What's my problem?</i>

00:05:58.030 --> 00:05:59.330
<i>What is my problem?!</i>

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:08.420
We will now decide the 
third round match-ups.

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:10.810
<i>I can't get all worked up.</i>

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:14.420
<i>Think of all those ugly matches 
where I lost to myself!</i>

00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:16.800
<i>But it's no use.</i>

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:15.890
Ichikawa Yuuna

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:17.230
Mashima Taichi

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:25.220
<i>I don't think I could face Arata 
in a match and not get worked up.</i>

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:28.750
<i>Individual matches may be team matches,</i>

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:30.200
<i>but I'm...</i>

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:33.290
<i>too preoccupied with my own issues.</i>

00:06:40.280 --> 00:06:41.410
Hanano-san!

00:06:42.070 --> 00:06:45.380
Sorry I'm late. How's everyone doing?

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:46.960
We're winning, Ms. Miyauchi!

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:48.760
The fourth round is next!

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:51.020
Ayase's not in peak form,

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:53.590
but she's somehow managing to squeak through.

00:06:53.590 --> 00:06:55.710
Mashima-senpai's doing his best, too!

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:58.600
He's had unusually good 
luck with his match-ups.

00:06:58.600 --> 00:06:59.550
I see.

00:07:01.430 --> 00:07:03.320
We will be deciding the match-ups shortly.

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:06.600
Ms. Sakurazawa!

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:11.610
I hear you helped my students 
during summer vacation.

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:13.430
I wanted to thank you.

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:15.250
No, I should thank you.

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:17.280
They're very promising students.

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:18.590
I learned a great deal from them.

00:07:19.640 --> 00:07:24.450
If I may ask, you're an experienced
karuta player, correct?

00:07:24.450 --> 00:07:25.670
Yes, that's right.

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:27.410
I'm embarrassed to admit it,

00:07:27.410 --> 00:07:29.920
but this is my second year 
as a karuta club adviser,

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:32.080
and I haven't even memorized 
the hundred poems.

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:36.100
I'm more scientific-minded, you see,
so it's not my strong suit...

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:38.330
I have no hope of giving 
them guidance in karuta.

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:40.760
All I can really do is 
protect their club room.

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:41.570
I see...

00:07:43.450 --> 00:07:44.560
So...

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:51.790
Do you think Ayase has what 
it takes to be the Queen?

00:07:57.480 --> 00:08:00.330
<i>Coach Harada and Hiroshi-san 
have been winning so far.</i>

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:02.330
<i>Taichi, too.</i>

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:05.080
<i>Taichi's amazing.</i>

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:07.000
<i>It's his first Class A tournament...</i>

00:08:09.570 --> 00:08:10.870
<i>And I...</i>

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:13.010
We have the match-ups for the fourth round.

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:14.850
Please be sure to take a look.

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:18.390
Yamamoto Yumi 
(Suihoku Society)

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:18.390
Wataya Arata 
(Fukui Nagumo Society)

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:19.140
Tachikawa Ririka 
(Sendai Fuyuki Society)

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:19.140
Harada Hidehiro 
(Shiranami Society)

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:19.890
.     Sudo Akita                         Yamashiro Rion 
(Hokuo Karuta Society)          (Fujisaki High School)

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:20.560
Shiroyama Koki 
(Hokuo Karuta Society)

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:20.560
Mashima Taichi 
(Shiranami Society)

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:25.150
Mashima Taichi 
(Shiranami Society)

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:25.150
Shiroyama Koki 
(Hokuo Karuta Society)

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:25.150
Sudo Akita                      Yamashiro Rion 
(Hokuo Karuta Society)    (Fujisaki High School)

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:25.150
Tachikawa Ririka                                   Yamamoto Yumi  
(Sendai Fuyuki Society)                          (Suihoku Society)

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:25.150
Harada Hidehiro 
(Shiranami Society)

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:25.150
Wataya Arata 
(Fukui Nagumo Society)

00:08:21.340 --> 00:08:23.380
That's the round of 16 for you!

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:25.130
This is getting intense!

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:26.600
Who's Chihaya-chan playing?

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:31.610
<b>Kotoki-in University
Karuta Society</b>

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:31.600
The runner-up Master, Takemura, grade 6!

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:36.130
I remember him. He was soundly 
defeated by Master Suo.

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:38.240
He came all the way from Shikoku?

00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:42.990
<i>Rion...</i>

00:08:43.780 --> 00:08:46.170
<i>I remember you.</i>

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:49.160
<i>Your game sense is incredible, but...</i>

00:08:49.450 --> 00:08:53.180
<i>when your rhythm is broken, you lose focus.</i>

00:08:53.180 --> 00:08:54.670
<i>My favorite prey.</i>

00:08:58.110 --> 00:09:01.170
You know, I've always wondered...

00:09:01.170 --> 00:09:04.830
Why do you always wear those curly hairpins?

00:09:04.830 --> 00:09:07.760
Oh, you noticed? It's pretty creepy, right?

00:09:07.760 --> 00:09:11.180
I tend to move around like this 
a lot. Makes you dizzy, right?

00:09:11.180 --> 00:09:12.320
Hey, wait...

00:09:14.230 --> 00:09:16.610
One on each side might be even creepier!

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:19.020
What do you think? What do you think?

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:22.610
<i>I have the luck of the draw today!</i>

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:28.280
<i>Which one? Which match should I focus on?</i>

00:09:28.280 --> 00:09:31.280
<i>Yumin, Mashima, and Ayase
are all in separate matches.</i>

00:09:31.280 --> 00:09:32.500
<i>What do I do?!</i>

00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:33.750
What?

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:36.310
K-Kana-chan?

00:09:36.670 --> 00:09:40.910
<i>I have no idea who I should 
cheer for, either.</i>

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:42.490
<i>But that's why...</i>

00:09:43.230 --> 00:09:46.270
<i>Full-time reader Igarashi Osamu, grade 7.</i>

00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:51.650
<i>A top reader, and the one whose voice 
is on the CDs we use in practice.</i>

00:09:52.210 --> 00:09:53.750
<i>His rhythm is precise,</i>

00:09:53.750 --> 00:09:56.770
<i>and his voice has a resonance and 
inflection that women can't replicate.</i>

00:09:57.100 --> 00:09:58.640
<i>This will be a learning experience.</i>

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:03.900
<i>A stopwatch?!</i>

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:08.170
Taking notes

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:07.610
<i>His precise rhythm is backed 
by precise self-verification!</i>

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:08.170
Tweet, tweet

00:10:07.610 --> 00:10:09.920
<i>This will be an amazing learning experience!</i>

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:09.170
<b>Tweet</b>

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:11.170
Igarashi Osamu 
At the Yoshino Tournament.
 I'll be reading, so more later.
 My throat's in great shape. 
I'll do my best (*^o^*)

00:10:17.570 --> 00:10:20.480
<i>I only saw the match on TV,</i>

00:10:20.480 --> 00:10:23.610
<i>and even I was discouraged when 
I saw how strong Master Suo was.</i>

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:27.530
<i>But...</i>

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:29.520
<i>But still...</i>

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:33.750
<i>Ayase, you need to get back on your feet!</i>

00:10:33.750 --> 00:10:35.290
<i>Come on, Mashima!</i>

00:10:35.290 --> 00:10:36.480
<i>Mashima-senpai!</i>

00:10:36.970 --> 00:10:38.140
It's time.

00:10:42.730 --> 00:10:51.160
<i>Naniwa Bay, now the flower 
blooms, but for winter</i>

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:59.660
<i>Here comes spring, 
now the flower blooms</i>

00:10:52.240 --> 00:10:55.470
<i>This resonance... Such powerful waves!</i>

00:10:56.150 --> 00:10:58.850
<i>They reach every last 
corner of this huge room!</i>

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:00.550
<i>He's amazing!</i>

00:11:01.700 --> 00:11:11.200
<i>Here comes spring, 
now the flower blooms</i>

00:11:12.180 --> 00:11:14.300
<i>My life means nothing...</i>

00:11:14.300 --> 00:11:16.140
<i>A mountain stream dips...</i>

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:20.290
<i>Takemura-san still goes after 
cards like a heavy tank.</i>

00:11:20.290 --> 00:11:23.580
<i>His sweeping attacks
make girls in particular flinch.</i>

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:28.080
<i>Ayase, you're swinging too much!</i>

00:11:28.760 --> 00:11:30.070
<i>Calm down!</i>

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:35.000
<i>May I live to see...</i>

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:37.190
<i>Gust of wind...</i>

00:11:37.190 --> 00:11:37.750
Damn!

00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:39.090
<i>Huh?</i>

00:11:39.400 --> 00:11:42.470
<i>That's one of her best cards, but there 
was hardly any force to her grab.</i>

00:11:42.910 --> 00:11:44.100
<i>But she still got it...</i>

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:48.020
You! Keep it down!

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:50.020
Oh! I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:11:53.050 --> 00:11:56.430
<i>Ms. Miyauchi's tasuki...</i>

00:11:59.560 --> 00:12:01.110
Ms. Miyauchi...

00:12:01.960 --> 00:12:03.940
Why did you ask me that question?

00:12:04.670 --> 00:12:06.950
If she could be Queen, I mean.

00:12:09.310 --> 00:12:11.810
She loves karuta.

00:12:11.810 --> 00:12:15.900
I knew that already, but then I 
came to see how serious she was.

00:12:16.690 --> 00:12:19.060
Her grades at school are below average.

00:12:19.060 --> 00:12:20.980
No, just barely above poor.

00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:24.640
She always says her best subject is PE.

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:26.480
I'm so worried for her future...

00:12:27.440 --> 00:12:30.470
But you can't be a professional karuta player.

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:36.730
I want to know what I can do to help her.

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:42.740
Fourth Future Plans Questionnaire
Year 2 Class 9 
Name: Ayase Chihaya

00:12:42.740 --> 00:12:44.800
I want to encourage her 
to pursue her dreams...

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:49.090
Her dream of being the Queen, 
and her dream for the future.

00:12:53.810 --> 00:12:54.500
<i>Wait, no!</i>

00:12:55.220 --> 00:12:57.120
<i>It's not that she's lost her force!</i>

00:12:58.970 --> 00:13:01.710
<i>She's just not using excessive 
strength anymore,</i>

00:13:01.710 --> 00:13:04.230
<i>since she was resting her 
right arm for so long!</i>

00:13:09.310 --> 00:13:10.420
<i>Shinobu-chan...</i>

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:13.460
<i>It's just beyond here, right?</i>

00:13:15.970 --> 00:13:18.220
<i>The truth of silent karuta...</i>

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:30.270
<i>The fall paddy shacks have rough thatching</i>

00:13:24.810 --> 00:13:27.540
<i>He leaned so far forward 
to put pressure on her!</i>

00:13:27.540 --> 00:13:30.090
<i>He doesn't want to let Ririka-chan 
play karuta her own way.</i>

00:13:30.090 --> 00:13:31.930
<i>Using full strength against a kid...</i>

00:13:32.230 --> 00:13:38.630
<i>My only thought as the boat 
takes me out to sea is that</i>

00:13:36.110 --> 00:13:40.030
I'm fairly certain I touched the card first.

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:44.210
<i>It's all yours.</i>

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:47.230
<i>He doesn't argue at all.</i>

00:13:47.590 --> 00:13:49.710
<i>He strives to play clean</i>

00:13:49.710 --> 00:13:51.810
<i>and avoids using excess energy.</i>

00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:56.780
<i>But did you know that giving no 
response at all uses energy, too?</i>

00:13:56.780 --> 00:13:58.860
<i>Swift waters parted...</i>

00:13:58.860 --> 00:14:00.340
<i>Mashima-senpai did it!</i>

00:14:00.340 --> 00:14:02.770
<i>He's gotten faster with 
the one-syllable cards!</i>

00:14:02.770 --> 00:14:04.520
<i>The tail feathers...</i>

00:14:04.520 --> 00:14:06.520
<i>My fear is not...</i>

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:08.970
Right, then...

00:14:08.970 --> 00:14:10.150
<i>What's going on with him?</i>

00:14:10.880 --> 00:14:14.710
<i>His hands are slow, and he 
doesn't seem all that athletic.</i>

00:14:14.710 --> 00:14:15.650
<i>But...</i>

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:19.790
<i>If I don't do everything perfectly,
he takes the card.</i>

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:22.160
<i>Perfectly...</i>

00:14:25.250 --> 00:14:26.850
Must be rough.

00:14:27.030 --> 00:14:27.780
Huh?

00:14:27.780 --> 00:14:30.310
It's harder to hear when 
you're tired, right?

00:14:31.270 --> 00:14:35.050
It must be rough having so many 
mental and physical weaknesses.

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:38.410
<i>It's her fourth match.</i>

00:14:38.840 --> 00:14:41.450
<i>When it's been six hours since 
the start of the event,</i>

00:14:39.100 --> 00:14:44.360
Man, I want to take her place...

00:14:41.450 --> 00:14:44.270
<i>the condition of each player starts to vary.</i>

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:47.670
<i>Some hit their first peak of exhaustion.</i>

00:14:48.350 --> 00:14:50.950
<i>Some get tired of memorizing and lose focus.</i>

00:14:51.480 --> 00:14:54.710
<i>Some finish warming up and 
start to move better.</i>

00:14:55.270 --> 00:14:59.340
<i>Some finally adjust to their 
kimono or right hand.</i>

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:04.650
<i>She's not wasting any movements!</i>

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:06.960
<i>Her hand-eye coordination is getting better.</i>

00:15:07.910 --> 00:15:09.900
<i>There's no way she even realizes it.</i>

00:15:10.530 --> 00:15:14.540
<i>She doesn't, but practicing with 
her left hand all that time</i>

00:15:14.540 --> 00:15:17.350
<i>resulted in mirroring her 
body and attack positions.</i>

00:15:18.170 --> 00:15:22.390
<i>Going after her old weak spots, her own 
left side and the opponent's right,</i>

00:15:22.390 --> 00:15:25.320
<i>broadened her awareness of 
where her right hand is going!</i>

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:30.010
<i>You have plenty of stamina, Ayase-san.</i>

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:39.870
<i>while snow falls upon my sleeves</i>

00:15:37.030 --> 00:15:39.530
<i>Some keep getting better as the day goes on,</i>

00:15:40.190 --> 00:15:41.270
<i>and...</i>

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:42.790
<i>the red that is the Tatsuta River</i>

00:15:42.390 --> 00:15:50.290
<i>Impassionate gods have never seen</i>

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:57.840
This is the wrong one.

00:15:57.840 --> 00:15:59.780
Who had "Impassionate" number 7?

00:15:59.780 --> 00:16:01.360
Who had "Impassionate" number 11—

00:16:01.360 --> 00:16:02.220
Oh.

00:16:02.220 --> 00:16:03.350
Thanks.

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:04.480
Thank you.

00:16:05.680 --> 00:16:07.480
<i>Their cards collided.</i>

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:12.240
<i>the red that is the Tatsuta River</i>

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:11.950
<i>They both took "Impassionate" 
with the same speed.</i>

00:16:13.750 --> 00:16:15.620
<i>This really is rough.</i>

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:17.700
<i>I haven't played any official 
matches in so long.</i>

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:21.410
<i>My boobs are getting tight, too. 
Why'd they have to be so productive?</i>

00:16:21.760 --> 00:16:24.700
<i>But I'm finally in tune now.</i>

00:16:25.700 --> 00:16:30.010
<i>And some finally complete their 
ear tuning in the fourth match.</i>

00:16:30.740 --> 00:16:32.500
<i>You can do it, Mom!</i>

00:16:32.500 --> 00:16:34.380
<i>I feel that my love...</i>

00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:36.130
<i>Note that though...</i>

00:16:36.130 --> 00:16:39.020
<i>That's the former Queen 
Inokuma, grade 6, for you.</i>

00:16:39.020 --> 00:16:42.610
<i>If not for those two maternity leaves, 
she'd have kept her streak going.</i>

00:16:42.610 --> 00:16:43.900
<i>Is she back in action?</i>

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:45.990
<i>Inokuma, grade 6...</i>

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:48.750
<i>Five years younger than me, and my rival.</i>

00:16:49.500 --> 00:16:51.690
<i>I challenged her four times,</i>

00:16:51.690 --> 00:16:53.530
<i>but I couldn't win once.</i>

00:16:54.390 --> 00:16:56.870
How did you get so good?

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:59.670
Oh, I can take cards because 
I hear well, that's all.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:03.400
If you can hear better, 
you can take them, too!

00:17:03.820 --> 00:17:05.960
<i>She's a different sort 
of genius than Suo-san:</i>

00:17:06.470 --> 00:17:08.430
<i>the honest, up-front type.</i>

00:17:10.570 --> 00:17:12.420
<i>This is not going to end well.</i>

00:17:13.780 --> 00:17:16.820
<i>I thought his overall 
movements were too heavy,</i>

00:17:16.820 --> 00:17:19.840
<i>but since his hands are slow,
he just doesn't need to stop himself.</i>

00:17:20.280 --> 00:17:23.190
<i>This is bad.
 He's grabbing everything with precision.</i>

00:17:25.290 --> 00:17:27.110
<i>Crush Mashima.</i>

00:17:27.550 --> 00:17:29.670
<i>Drain his stamina and energy.</i>

00:17:32.140 --> 00:17:33.220
<i>Sudo-san...</i>

00:17:33.830 --> 00:17:35.750
<i>Make sure Sudo-san wins!</i>

00:17:36.040 --> 00:17:38.240
<i>Make him do that condescending laugh of his!</i>

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:38.240
<b>Keh-heh-heh</b>

00:17:39.140 --> 00:17:42.820
<i>He's doing this for his team, too...</i>

00:18:00.860 --> 00:18:03.080
<i>I know how you feel.</i>

00:18:04.230 --> 00:18:06.640
<i>It's nice to have a senpai, isn't it?</i>

00:18:11.350 --> 00:18:13.310
<i>Feel love deepen...</i>

00:18:13.870 --> 00:18:15.800
<i>He's typically slow, right?</i>

00:18:17.290 --> 00:18:20.460
<i>So I just need to cover 
my cards or block him.</i>

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:23.250
<i>I don't need to take every card perfectly.</i>

00:18:23.800 --> 00:18:26.360
<i>My body feels lighter!</i>

00:18:29.770 --> 00:18:32.080
<i>I'm not as far ahead as I thought I'd be.</i>

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:33.980
<i>Even though she's exhausted...</i>

00:18:34.830 --> 00:18:38.050
<i>That narrow-eyes jerk! 
I'll clobber him myself someday!</i>

00:18:35.740 --> 00:18:42.140
<i>...the troubles of this world</i>

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:46.150
<i>All alone...</i>

00:18:51.800 --> 00:18:54.790
<i>How can she still take
her best cards so quickly?</i>

00:18:56.390 --> 00:18:57.910
<i>Some people hear more clearly</i>

00:18:58.450 --> 00:19:00.560
<i>the more tired they are!</i>

00:19:02.360 --> 00:19:04.430
<i>I don't care about being Queen.</i>

00:19:04.430 --> 00:19:08.530
<i>I just want to get my rice and 
defend Fujisaki's reputation.</i>

00:19:09.310 --> 00:19:10.380
<i>But...</i>

00:19:10.860 --> 00:19:11.870
<i>But...</i>

00:19:12.220 --> 00:19:14.370
Yama-chan! Let's have some good games!

00:19:16.530 --> 00:19:19.030
That means we're practicing 
for the Queen match!

00:19:26.450 --> 00:19:28.170
Thank you very much.

00:19:29.540 --> 00:19:30.890
<i>I'm beat...</i>

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:33.230
<i>What the hell was that? She's just a girl!</i>

00:19:39.150 --> 00:19:40.400
<b>Throb</b>

00:19:44.290 --> 00:19:46.110
Yes! Arata-kun did it!

00:19:46.350 --> 00:19:48.300
Thank you very much.

00:19:48.980 --> 00:19:50.720
You almost had it, Yumin.

00:19:50.720 --> 00:19:53.370
But it doesn't matter.
The real fight is in two weeks.

00:19:53.760 --> 00:19:56.610
So what was Wataya Arata like?

00:19:56.610 --> 00:19:58.910
I got the sense that he's still young.

00:19:59.640 --> 00:20:02.240
If I could have argued 
about four more cards,

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:05.140
<b>Inexplicably
fatigued</b>

00:20:02.240 --> 00:20:05.250
I could have thrown him 
off his pace completely.

00:20:06.690 --> 00:20:07.860
<i>Chihaya...</i>

00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:09.300
<i>Takemura-san...</i>

00:20:09.940 --> 00:20:12.630
<i>After I lost so bad in the Master match,</i>

00:20:12.630 --> 00:20:14.850
<i>I couldn't play karuta for half a year.</i>

00:20:15.200 --> 00:20:18.470
I saw you on TV! I hope 
you try again someday!

00:20:18.470 --> 00:20:20.290
I'll be looking forward to it!

00:20:20.980 --> 00:20:22.320
<i>Half a year...</i>

00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:25.440
<i>What was I doing for half a year?!</i>

00:20:27.570 --> 00:20:31.590
<i>Half a year is all it takes for such
a talented young player to show up!</i>

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:36.300
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:20:36.750 --> 00:20:38.030
<i>She did it!</i>

00:20:38.030 --> 00:20:40.290
<i>The quarterfinalists have been decided!</i>

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:42.570
The Shiranami Society still 
has four players continuing!

00:20:42.570 --> 00:20:44.110
And the Nagumo Society has two!

00:20:44.110 --> 00:20:45.560
The Shiranami Society has the edge!

00:20:45.790 --> 00:20:48.050
The high school kids have 
been amazing this year.

00:20:48.050 --> 00:20:50.550
We will now decide the 
quarterfinal match-ups.

00:20:48.370 --> 00:20:50.040
How's this going to end?

00:20:50.730 --> 00:20:52.010
The Prez won, too!

00:20:52.010 --> 00:20:52.820
He won!

00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:57.390
Part of it is up to fate and the times,

00:20:58.380 --> 00:21:02.150
so I don't know if Ayase-san 
can become Queen, but...

00:21:03.990 --> 00:21:04.530
<b>Ayase Chihaya</b>

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:05.410
<b>Harada
Hidehiro</b>

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:06.660
<b>Ba-dump</b>

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:06.660
<b>Oho?</b>

00:21:06.870 --> 00:21:08.560
Oh, you're from the same society.

00:21:08.560 --> 00:21:09.420
I'll draw again.

00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:13.030
<i>Will it be Sudo-san, Murao-san...</i>

00:21:14.560 --> 00:21:15.540
<i>or Arata?</i>

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:16.670
<i>Harada Hidehiro                               Ayase Chihaya</i>

00:21:16.670 --> 00:21:18.290
<i>Inokuma Haruka</i>

00:21:25.630 --> 00:21:28.830
There's someone she'll have to defeat first.
